 "summary": "s24vmm --fp-on sets CPACR_EL1=0x300000 on the boot vCPU before its first KVM_RUN and reports fp_on in the start event; without the option, behaviour is unchanged. check.py passes on 368e146: test_vmm 220 and test_io 92 checks under ASan+UBSan, TSan, and a warning-free static NDK build. The reason: XNU common_start writes CPACR_EL1 with no ISB after it (start.s:762-763), and the VM-054 fp-sync probe shows that an FP instruction after an unsynchronized FPEN write still traps on the S24 cores.",
